VI  - 13
IP  - 2
DP  - 2023 Jan 28
TI  - Robotic Bronchoscopy: Review of Three Systems.
LID - 10.3390/life13020354 [doi]
LID - 354
AB  - Robotic bronchoscopy (RB) has been shown to improve access to smaller and more 
      peripheral lung lesions, while simultaneously staging the mediastinum. 
      Pre-clinical studies demonstrated extremely high diagnostic yields, but 
      real-world RB yields have yet to fully matched up in prospective studies. Despite 
      this, RB technology has rapidly evolved and has great potential for lung-cancer 
      diagnosis and even treatment. In this article, we review the historical and 
      present challenges with RB in order to compare three RB systems.
