AB  - The 55th SEPAR Congress was held in Pamplona from 2 to 4 of June 2022. Once 
      again, it was the referral scientific meeting for specialists in pulmonology, 
      thoracic surgery, nursing, physiotherapy, paediatric respiratory diseases and 
      other disciplines involved in respiratory care. The Spanish Society of 
      Pulmonology and Thoracic Surgery showed its national and international leadership 
      in the management of respiratory diseases, which was reflected in a program with 
      an excellent content and a high scientific level. In this review, we offer a 
      summary of some notable aspects covered in six selected areas of interest: 
      pulmonary vascular diseases, non-invasive mechanical ventilation and sleep 
      disorders, asthma, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), interstitial 
      lung diseases (ILD), and interventional pulmonolgy and lung transplant.
