TI  - Partnership with Interventional Pulmonologist: An Anesthesiologist's Perspective.
PG  - 1049-1063
LID - S0030-6665(19)30149-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.otc.2019.08.006 [doi]
AB  - Via the emergence of new bronchoscopic technologies and techniques, there is 
      enormous growth in the number of procedures being performed in nonoperating room 
      settings. This, coupled with a greater focus from the Centers for Medicare and 
      Medicaid Services for mandated anesthesiology oversight of procedural sedation 
      for bronchoscopy by the pulmonologists has led to a more frequent working 
      partnership between interventional pulmonologists and anesthesiologists. This 
      article offers the interventional pulmonologist insight into how the 
      anesthesiologist thinks and approaches anesthetic care delivery.
