TI  - The Business of Bronchoscopy: How to Set up an Interventional Pulmonology 
      Program.
PG  - 239-243
LID - S0272-5231(17)30117-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2017.11.006 [doi]
AB  - Interventional pulmonology has advanced rapidly over the last decade and 
      continues to evolve with new medical advances and changes in the health care 
      landscape. Establishing and developing a new interventional pulmonology program 
      entails careful planning, including a needs assessment, a business plan with 
      financial and marketing considerations, and outcomes monitoring. Addressing these 
      aspects will provide a framework to ensure the success of a new interventional 
      pulmonology program that can provide valuable services to the local practice and 
      community.
