TI  - Interventional Pulmonology Procedures in the Intensive Care Unit.
PG  - 359-372
LID - S0272-5231(25)00015-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2025.02.013 [doi]
AB  - The intensive care unit (ICU) is often occupied by patients with high-acuity 
      disease processes in which there are likely numerous opportunities interventional 
      pulmonologist (IP) to help manage with their intensivist colleagues. The capacity 
      to evaluate and support numerous disease states commonly seen in the ICU, such as 
      respiratory failure, airway obstruction, hemoptysis, and so forth can often lead 
      to a strong collaboration and active participation in the care of many different 
      patient populations within the ICU. We plan to review and summarize the most 
      common ICU procedures that may be performed by IPs.
