TI  - The Art of Rigid Bronchoscopy and Airway Stenting.
PG  - 149-167
LID - S0272-5231(17)30122-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2017.11.011 [doi]
AB  - Interventional pulmonology has grown significantly over the last 2 decades and is 
      now seen as an essential component in thoracic oncology care. The rigid 
      bronchoscope occupies a central role in this specialty and offers many important 
      advantages over the flexible scope when performing therapeutic procedures on 
      central airways. Although stenting practices have evolved, it is generally 
      accepted that stents offer an important treatment option for selected patients 
      with benign and malignant airway diseases. This article discusses rigid 
      bronchoscopy and stenting, future challenges, complications of the procedure and 
      stents, and future directions.
