TI  - Interventional pulmonology procedures: an update.
PG  - 121-9
AB  - Bronchoscopy is the most important tool in diagnosis of respiratory diseases, but 
      also provides therapeutic options in various disorders. Besides hemoptysis, 
      airway stenoses are a frequent indication for therapeutic bronchoscopy 
      interventions. Thereby, a broad spectrum of endoscopic techniques including 
      electrocautery, argon plasma coagulation, laser treatment, cryosurgery and stent 
      implantation is available. In the last decade, development of new endoscopic 
      modalities provides also treatment of patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary 
      disease and uncontrolled asthma.
