TI  - [Endobronchial metastases secondary to extrapulmonary malignancies].
PG  - 219-224
LID - 10.5578/tt.68301 [doi]
AB  - Although parenchymal, pleural and mediastinal lymph node locations of metastatic 
      Lung cancer are frequently seen, they are rarely found endobronchially. 
      Endobronchial metastases comprise a portion of central airway obstructions that 
      are diagnosed and treated by interventional pulmonology. Interventional 
      procedures for endobronchial metastases (EBM) can help us reach early diagnosis, 
      or in advanced cases with respiratory symptoms, used palliatively.
