VI  - 17
IP  - 744-2
DP  - 2021 Jun 30
TI  - [Flexible bronchoscopy: contribution of the anesthesiologis].
PG  - 1269-1272
AB  - The field of interventional pulmonology is expanding rapidly with increasingly 
      complex endoscopic procedures. Pulmonologists and anesthesiologists are both 
      airway specialists. When they cooperate in performing flexible bronchoscopies, 
      they must share a common anatomical space. A close and dynamic collaboration 
      helps to optimize patient management by enhancing safety, facilitating the 
      procedures and improving patient satisfaction. Several challenges are to be taken 
      up, notably managing frail and often polymorbid patients, working outside the 
      usual operating-room area, and the need to be quickly available, given the 
      frequently semi-urgent setting of these procedures. In this context, the 
      optimization of collaborative procedures is essential.
