TI  - Medical thoracoscopy without pleural fluid: How I do it.
LID - 10.4081/monaldi.2021.1331 [doi]
AB  - Thoracoscopy is a commonly used minimally invasive procedure in the field of 
      interventional pulmonology. While medical thoracoscopy is the widely preferred 
      modality, modifications to the technique and expansion in the scope of its 
      utility have always challenged the conventional approach. We describe a modified 
      technique of medical thoracoscopy in absence of pleural effusion also known as 
      dry thoracoscopy under sedation and local anaesthesia.
