TI  - Novel technique of performing transbronchial lung cryobiopsy (TBLC) for 
      diagnosing diffuse parenchymal lung diseases (DPLD) in infants.
PG  - e01096
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.1096 [doi]
LID - e01096
AB  - Childhood interstitial lung disease (ChILD) diagnosis often requires surgical 
      lung biopsy after the common causes are ruled out. However, surgical lung biopsy 
      has its own set of complications. Hence transbronchial lung cryobiopsy has been 
      used in various studies of adult interstitial lung disease (ILD) with good yield 
      and minimal complications. But this newer mode is rarely used in diagnosing 
      children with suspected ILD. Here, we present the first case of the use of this 
      technique in an infant via a rigid tracheoscope.
