DP  - 2018 Sep-Oct
TI  - Use of dedicated optical tracheal dilator for postintubation tracheal stenosis: 
      First report from India.
PG  - 417-420
LID - 10.4103/lungindia.lungindia_372_17 [doi]
AB  - Postintubation tracheal stenosis is preventable yet commonly occurring clinical 
      condition. Early in the disease, nonspecific symptoms may predominate but once 
      the stenosis reaches a critical stage life-threatening respiratory compromise may 
      ensue. Bronchoscopic interventions are an invaluable tool in the management both 
      as a primary treatment and as an interim procedure before the surgery. Optical 
      dilatational tracheoscopy is a safe and minimally invasive procedure in the 
      treatment of benign tracheal stenosis. Involvement of multidisciplinary team 
      early in the treatment planning gives the best possible results.
